  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-priority question is whether the full multimodal + multiprofile architecture with the strongest encoders can achieve high validation accuracy, establishing a performance ceiling for the search. config_005 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) combines the most expressive RNA encoder (scgpt foundation model), the most powerful image encoder (large ViT), the most flexible aggregation (transformer over multiple profiles), and a simple concat fusion. Testing this first gives a strong reference point: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate components to identify which are essential; if it underperforms, we learn that the full architecture is not the right direction and can pivot to cheaper or alternative designs. This is the most expensive configuration in the set (scgpt + ViT-L + transformer aggregation over multiple profiles), but as experiment 1 of 10, establishing the ceiling is the best use of a single slot to guide the remaining 9 experiments efficiently."
}

